From 2aec517eb92d4f09385769ff87be8572bf55f9dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dylanoliverdo-coder
 <265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:27:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(sim): the field cylinder gate counts cells as the
 column block does

Review of #4013: Dexel::block now counts with cells_across, and the
field arm's cylinder gate still used the plain ceiling. A round 4096
cells across, read two ulps long, passed the column gate and was refused
by the field gate as 4097x4097, against the backend-independent refusal
law. The field cylinder gate now uses cells_across.

Pins: both cylinder gates at that boundary (the column arm builds it;
the field arm passes the grid gate and then refuses by name on its own
per-facet cell budget, as it does for any round that wide), one real part
of a cell more refused by both in the same words, and the field box gate
at the 4096-cell boundary. Each fails when its gate goes back to the
plain ceiling.

Fixes #4012

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
