From 9bb474804f5795eeef5952b81e8c2b60f55ceec0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dylanoliverdo-coder
 <265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:04:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(sim): every stock lattice counts its cells by the one
 rule

Review of #4013 asks for one rule that closes the class, not the one
case. The class: a stock or verdict lattice sized from a length, where an
edge a few ulps past a whole number of cells gains a sliver column. The
rule: such a count goes through cells_across, and an origin-locked
lattice takes its edge cells by edge_cells, the same law for an edge
coordinate.

Sites brought under it, beside the block, field box, field cylinder and
exact carry already on it:
- march lattice_of, the field arm's verdict lattice: a box 12.7 mm two
  ulps long had 51 columns there against the column arm's 50.
- carry_side, the side-on slabs of a cut body: 51 slabs, 50 on the
  exact carry of the same block.
- from_facets on both arms: 53 columns where the count plus its margin
  is 52, and a strip 4094 cells a few ulps long refused as 4097.

Pins, one per site; each fails on the old count (51, 51, 53) and passes
on the rule. Measurement grids that hold no stock are left as they are:
the edge-break window divides by a power of two (exact), and the scan
envelope has a full margin of air beyond the part.

Refs #4012

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
